<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Brittany</h1><p class="st-meta">851 CE – 939 CE (approx.) · capital Vannes</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Breton kingdom forged in the 9th century by Nominoe and his successors, who won independence from the Carolingian Franks.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-pious">Louis the Pious</a> appointed the Breton noble <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nominoe">Nominoe</a> as his representative in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-brittany">Brittany</a> in 831. After Louis's death Nominoe broke with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a>, defeating him at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ballon">Ballon</a> in 845. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erispoe">Erispoe</a> won again at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-jengland">Jengland</a> in 851, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-angers-851">Treaty of Angers</a> recognised him as king with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rennes">Rennes</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nantes">Nantes</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pays-de-retz">Pays de Retz</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom united <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/domnonee">Domnonée</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cornouaille">Cornouaille</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/broerec">Broërec</a> with the Frankish marches. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salomon-of-brittany">Salomon</a>, who killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erispoe">Erispoe</a> and took the throne in 857, gained the Cotentin and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avranchin">Avranchin</a> in 867. The kings ruled through local machtierns and monasteries such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/redon-abbey">Redon</a>, and set up a Breton church province at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dol-de-bretagne">Dol</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After internal conflict <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alan-i-king-of-brittany">Alan the Great</a> defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-questembert">Questembert</a> around 888, but after his death in 907 Vikings overran <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-brittany">Brittany</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alan-ii-duke-of-brittany">Alan Barbetorte</a> returned from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in 936 and expelled them by 939, ruling as duke and founding the Duchy of Brittany.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-brittany.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Brittany" width="320" height="274"><figcaption>Image: (Sémhur; derivative work by Fab5669 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Kingdom_of_Brittany_845-867-fr.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>851 CE – 939 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vannes</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Erispoe, Salomon, Alan the Great</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Breton, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Breton Kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=895&amp;focus=kingdom-of-brittany" aria-label="Kingdom of Brittany on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4610 497 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Brittany lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4930 753L5054 728M4930 753L4964 777M4930 753L4905 753M4930 753L4936 764"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M4964 777h0M4905 753h0M4936 764h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4930 753h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4930 753h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot